# Orastery Woes (windurst 86): the qm1 and Eldhrimnir in Ro'Maeve with GM-set states. Available with the
# map (GM): no handler, nothing pops (the qm1's default NOTHING_OUT_OF_ORDINARY). Accepted without the map: nil. The
# map: Eldhrimnir pops; the map taken by GM before the kill: its death sets nothing, so the next qm1 talk (no map,
# killed_wsnm 0) is nil. The map again, and a wait for its body to go (popFromQM needs it despawned): it pops again;
# the quest deleted by GM (available) before the kill: no death handler, killed_wsnm not set; accepted again by GM,
# after the wait the qm1 (the map, killed_wsnm 0): it pops a third time, no Annals of Truth.
lists Romaeve/qm1/onTrigger
char zone=Romaeve pos=199.3,-8.1,-27.5 job=WAR lvl=75
login
keyitem MapToTheAnnalsOfTruth
trigger qm1                                         # available, the map: no handler; nothing pops; NOTHING_OUT_OF_ORDINARY
quest Windurst.OrasteryWoes accepted
delkeyitem MapToTheAnnalsOfTruth
trigger qm1                                         # accepted, no map: nil; NOTHING_OUT_OF_ORDINARY
keyitem MapToTheAnnalsOfTruth
trigger qm1                                         # the map: Eldhrimnir pops (claimed); SENSE_OMINOUS_PRESENCE
delkeyitem MapToTheAnnalsOfTruth
kill ELDHRIMNIR                                # no map: killed_wsnm not set
trigger qm1                                         # no map, killed_wsnm 0: nil; NOTHING_OUT_OF_ORDINARY
keyitem MapToTheAnnalsOfTruth
tick 15000                                          # its body despawns: one zone tick per tick statement
tick 15000
tick 15000
trigger qm1                                         # the map: it pops again; SENSE_OMINOUS_PRESENCE
quest Windurst.OrasteryWoes available
kill ELDHRIMNIR                                # the quest available: no death handler; killed_wsnm not set
quest Windurst.OrasteryWoes accepted
tick 15000
tick 15000
tick 15000
trigger qm1                                         # killed_wsnm 0, the map: it pops again; SENSE_OMINOUS_PRESENCE
